# Cloudflare Workers static assets are served from the whole repo root
# ([assets] directory = "./" in wrangler.toml), so anything NOT meant to
# be public needs to be listed here explicitly -- unlike .gitignore,
# this controls what's actually served to visitors, not just what's
# tracked in git. A real exposure was found and fixed 2026-08-08: /.git/
# was publicly fetchable (confirmed via a live curl returning 200),
# along with Android build artifacts that have no reason being served
# from the website at all.

.git/
.wrangler/
node_modules/

# Android app projects -- native source, build output, keystores. None
# of this belongs on the public website; the apps load web pages FROM
# this site, they don't get served BY it.
android-phone-app/
android-tv-app/

# Editor/OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
*.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local docs/scratch that shouldn't be public even though they're
# harmless if leaked -- keep the public site to just the actual app.
PROJECT_STATE.md
SUPPORT_PLAYBOOK.md
scratchpad/
